      Osa 5:
       
      Material
    </h2>
    
    
    <div
      className="e-grading-instructions-question e-mrg-b-8 e-clearfix"
      data-annotation-anchor="13"
      id="13"
    >
      <div
        className="anchor"
        id="question-nr-13"
      />
      <h3
        className="exam-question-title"
      >
        <strong
          className="exam-question-title__display-number"
        >
          13. 
        </strong>
        attachment
         
        <span
          className="e-score e-nowrap e-score--large e-font-size-l e-semibold"
        >
          0 p.
        </span>
      </h3>
      <div
        className="exam-question-instruction e-mrg-b-2"
        id="question-instruction-180"
      >
        
        
        <p>
          
          Questions can contain material like images, videos, HTML or files opened in external application.
          Reference data can be defined within the
          
          <code>
            e:attachment
          </code>
          
          by using
          
          <code>
            e:reference
          </code>
          
          element. Reference information is displayed by adding
          
          <code>
            e:references
          </code>
          
          element, usually at the end of the exam.
        
        </p>
        
        
        <p>
          
          If material should be
          displayed on an external material page, the
          
          <code>
            e:attachment
          </code>
          
          element can be defined
          as a child of an
          
          <code>
            e:external-material
          </code>
          
          element.
        
        </p>
        
        
        <p>
          
          
          <code>
            e:external-material
          </code>
          
          can be either a child of an
          
          <code>
            e:exam
          </code>
          
          or
          
          <code>
            e:question
          </code>
          
          element, depending on whether the material is exam-specific, or specific to a single question.
        
        </p>
        
      
      </div>
    </div>
    
    
    <div
      className="e-grading-instructions-question e-mrg-b-8 e-clearfix"
      data-annotation-anchor="14"
      id="14"
    >
      <div
        className="anchor"
        id="question-nr-14"
      />
      <h3
        className="exam-question-title"
      >
        <strong
          className="exam-question-title__display-number"
        >
          14. 
        </strong>
        image
         
        <span
          className="e-score e-nowrap e-score--large e-font-size-l e-semibold"
        >
          0 p.
        </span>
      </h3>
      <div
        className="exam-question-instruction e-mrg-b-2"
        id="question-instruction-181"
      >
        
        
        <code>
          e:image
        </code>
        
        element adds an image to the exam. It can be used anywhere where
        HTML is allowed.
      
      </div>
    </div>
    
    
    <div
      className="e-grading-instructions-question e-mrg-b-8 e-clearfix"
      data-annotation-anchor="15"
      id="15"
    >
      <div
        className="anchor"
        id="question-nr-15"
      />
      <h3
        className="exam-question-title"
      >
        <strong
          className="exam-question-title__display-number"
        >
          15. 
        </strong>
        image-overlay
         
        <span
          className="e-score e-nowrap e-score--large e-font-size-l e-semibold"
        >
          0 p.
        </span>
      </h3>
      <div
        className="exam-question-instruction e-mrg-b-2"
        id="question-instruction-182"
      >
        
        
        <p>
          
          
          <code>
            e:image-overlay
          </code>
          
          element can contain one or more image elements. It can be used anywhere where
        HTML is allowed. The images are rendered on top of each other, and an input slider
        is added for each image to allow for the adjustment of the opacity (transparency) of
        the image. The label for each input slider is taken from the text
        inside each
          
          <code>
            e:image
          </code>
          
          element. The text can be localized.
        
        </p>
        
        
        <p>
          Make sure that all the images have the same width
          and height in pixels. Differently sized images will cause unwanted layout effects.
        
        </p>
        
      
      </div>
    </div>
    
    
    <div
      className="e-grading-instructions-question e-mrg-b-8 e-clearfix"
      data-annotation-anchor="16"
      id="16"
    >
      <div
        className="anchor"
        id="question-nr-16"
      />
      <h3
        className="exam-question-title"
      >
        <strong
          className="exam-question-title__display-number"
        >
          16. 
        </strong>
        audio
         
        <span
          className="e-score e-nowrap e-score--large e-font-size-l e-semibold"
        >
          0 p.
        </span>
      </h3>
      <div
        className="exam-question-instruction e-mrg-b-2"
        id="question-instruction-183"
      >
        
        
        <code>
          e:audio
        </code>
        
        element adds an audio to the exam. It can be used anywhere where
          HTML is allowed.
      
      </div>
    </div>
    
    
    <div
      className="e-grading-instructions-question e-mrg-b-8 e-clearfix"
      data-annotation-anchor="17"
      id="17"
    >
      <div
        className="anchor"
        id="question-nr-17"
      />
      <h3
        className="exam-question-title"
      >
        <strong
          className="exam-question-title__display-number"
        >
          17. 
        </strong>
        audio-group
         
        <span
          className="e-score e-nowrap e-score--large e-font-size-l e-semibold"
        >
          6 p.
        </span>
      </h3>
      <div
        className="exam-question-instruction e-mrg-b-2"
        id="question-instruction-184"
      >
        
        
        <code>
          e:audio-group
        </code>
        
        element can be used to group audio elements by adding
        a separator before the group.
      
      </div>
      <div
        className="e-grading-instructions-question e-mrg-l-8 e-mrg-y-4"
        data-annotation-anchor="17.1"
        id="17.1"
      >
        <div
