            </div>
            
      
          </div>
          
      
          <div
            aria-description="Tähän kysymykseen ei ole vastattu"
            className="e-exam-question e-level-1 e-mrg-l-8 e-mrg-y-4 no-answer"
            id="1.1"
          >
            
        
            <h4
              className="exam-question-title e-normal e-font-size-m"
            >
              <strong
                className="exam-question-title__display-number exam-question-title__display-number--indented"
              >
                1.1 
              </strong>
              Special characters as entities
               
            </h4>
            
        
            <div
              className="exam-question-instruction e-mrg-b-2"
              id="question-instruction-168"
            >
              
          
              <p>
                Certain characters requires escaping as entities in exam XML documents
              </p>
              
          
              <table
                className="e-table"
              >
                <caption />
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>
                      Character
                    </th>
                    <th>
                      Notation
                    </th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td>
                      NBSP (non-breaking-space)
                    </td>
                    <td>
                      <code>
                        &#xA0;
                      </code>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>
                      SHY ­ (soft-hyphen)
                    </td>
                    <td>
                      <code>
                        &#173;
                      </code>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>
                      &gt;
                    </td>
                    <td>
                      <code>
                        &gt;
                      </code>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>
                      &lt;
                    </td>
                    <td>
                      <code>
                        &lt;
                      </code>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>
                      &
                    </td>
                    <td>
                      <code>
                        &amp;
                      </code>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
              
          
              <p>
                Notice, that e.g. 
                <code>
                  &nbsp;
                </code>
                 and 
                <code>
                  &shy;
                </code>
                 does not work.
              </p>
              
        
            </div>
            
      
          </div>
          
    
        </div>
        

    
        <div
          aria-description="Tähän kysymykseen ei ole vastattu"
          className="e-exam-question e-level-0 e-mrg-b-8 e-clearfix no-answer"
          id="2"
        >
          
      
          <h3
            className="exam-question-title"
          >
            <strong
              className="exam-question-title__display-number"
            >
              2. 
            </strong>
            Exam
             
          </h3>
          
      
          <div
            className="exam-question-instruction e-mrg-b-2"
            id="question-instruction-169"
          >
            
        
            <p>
              
          Top-level exam element.
        
            </p>
            
      
          </div>
          
      
          <table
            className="e-table e-width-full"
          >
            <caption>
              Element attributes
            </caption>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>
                  Attribute
                </th>
                <th>
                  Type
                </th>
                <th>
                  Mandatory
                </th>
                <th>
                  Default value
                </th>
                <th>
                  Description
                </th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>
                  exam-schema-version
                </td>
                <td>
                  Version string
                </td>
                <td>
                  No
                </td>
                <td>
                  —
                </td>
                <td>
                  Schema version, only 0.1 for now
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>
                  date
                </td>
                <td>
                  YYYY-MM-DD
                </td>
                <td>
                  No
                </td>
                <td>
                  —
                </td>
                <td>
                  Exam date
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>
                  exam-code
                </td>
                <td>
                  exam code string
                </td>
                <td>
                  No
                </td>
                <td>
                  —
                </td>
                <td>
                  Exam code used for exam specific translations
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>
                  day-code
                </td>
                <td>
                  exam day code string
                </td>
                <td>
                  No
                </td>
                <td>
                  —
                </td>
                <td>
                  Exam day code used for exam specific translations
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>
                  exam-stylesheet
                </td>
                <td>
                  custom CSS stylesheet file name
                </td>
                <td>
                  No
                </td>
                <td>
                  —
                </td>
                <td>
                  CSS file with this name must exist in attachments directory
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>
                  max-answers
                </td>
                <td>
                  Integer
                </td>
                <td>
                  No
                </td>
                <td>
                  No limit
                </td>
                <td>
                  Maximum number of questions student should answer
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>
                  meta
                </td>
                <td>
                  String
                </td>
                <td>
                  No
                </td>
                <td>
                  –
                </td>
                <td>
                  Metadata about element
                </td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          
      
          <p>
            
        
            <code>
              exam-code
            </code>
            
        and
        
            <code>
              day-code
            </code>
            
        attributes control exam-specific
        translations, e.g. the heading text of table of contents, and the exam title if specific
        
            <code>
              e:exam-title
            </code>
            
        element is missing. Currently supported exam and day
        code pairs can be found in
        
            <a
              href="https://github.com/digabi/exam-engine/blob/master/packages/mastering/src/i18n/exam_titles_fi-FI.json"
            >
              https://github.com/digabi/exam-engine/blob/master/packages/mastering/src/i18n/exam_titles_fi-FI.json
            </a>
            
        .
      
          </p>
          
      
          <div
            className="warning-box"
          >
            
        max-answers is ignored in Abitti grading.
      
          </div>
          
      
          <div
            aria-description="Tähän kysymykseen ei ole vastattu"
            className="e-exam-question e-level-1 e-mrg-l-8 e-mrg-y-4 no-answer"
            id="2.1"
          >
            
        
            <h4
              className="exam-question-title e-normal e-font-size-m"
            >
              <strong
                className="exam-question-title__display-number exam-question-title__display-number--indented"
              >
                2.1 
              </strong>
              Example
               
            </h4>
            
        
            <h4 />
            
        
            <pre
              className="code"
            >
              &lt;e:exam
  xmlns:e="http://ylioppilastutkinto.fi/exam.xsd"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://ylioppilastutkinto.fi/exam.xsd https://abitti.net/schema/exam.xsd"
  exam-schema-version="0.1"
  date="2018-09-29"
  exam-code="EA"
  exam-stylesheet="custom.css"&gt;
            </pre>
            
      
          </div>
          
    
        </div>
        

    
        <div
          aria-description="Tähän kysymykseen ei ole vastattu"
          className="e-exam-question e-level-0 e-mrg-b-8 e-clearfix no-answer"
          id="3"
        >
          
      
          <h3
            className="exam-question-title"
          >
            <strong
              className="exam-question-title__display-number"
            >
              3. 
            </strong>
            Languages and localization
             
          </h3>
          
      
          <div
            className="exam-question-instruction e-mrg-b-2"
            id="question-instruction-170"
          >
            
        
            <p>
              
          Content for multiple language versions of the same exam can be defined using localization elements.
        
            </p>
            
        
            <div
              className="warning-box"
            >
              
          Multiple languages work in Abitti when you create transfer zip with "npm run create-transfer-zip" -command. It generates separate transfer zip for each language.
        
            </div>
            
      
          </div>
          
      
          <div
            aria-description="Tähän kysymykseen ei ole vastattu"
            className="e-exam-question e-level-1 e-mrg-l-8 e-mrg-y-4 no-answer"
            id="3.1"
          >
            
        
            <h4
              className="exam-question-title e-normal e-font-size-m"
            >
              <strong
                className="exam-question-title__display-number exam-question-title__display-number--indented"
              >
                3.1 
              </strong>
              Example
               
            </h4>
            
        
            <h4 />
            
        
            <pre
              className="code"
            >
              &lt;e:languages&gt;
  &lt;e:language&gt;fi-FI&lt;/e:language&gt;
  &lt;e:language&gt;sv-FI&lt;/e:language&gt;
&lt;/e:languages&gt;
...
&lt;e:localization lang="fi-FI"&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;
    Älä jätä mitään merkintöjä sellaisen tehtävän vastaukselle varattuun tilaan,
    jota et halua jättää arvosteltavaksi.
  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/e:localization&gt;
&lt;e:localization lang="sv-FI"&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;
    Lämna inga anteckningar i svarsfältet för sådana uppgifter som du inte vill
    lämna in för bedömning.
  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/e:localization&gt;
            </pre>
            
        
            <span
              lang="fi-FI"
            >
              
          
              <p>
                
            Älä jätä mitään merkintöjä sellaisen tehtävän vastaukselle varattuun tilaan,
            jota et halua jättää arvosteltavaksi.
          
              </p>
              
        
            </span>
            
        
      
          </div>
          

      
          <div
            aria-description="Tähän kysymykseen ei ole vastattu"
            className="e-exam-question e-level-1 e-mrg-l-8 e-mrg-y-4 no-answer"
            id="3.2"
          >
            
        
            <h4
              className="exam-question-title e-normal e-font-size-m"
            >
              <strong
                className="exam-question-title__display-number exam-question-title__display-number--indented"
              >
                3.2 
              </strong>
              Pre-defined translations
               
            </h4>
            
        
            <p>
              There are some pre-defined translations that can be easily reused with the 
              <code>
                e:translation
              </code>
               tag. For example this code
            </p>
            
        
            <pre
              className="code"
            >
              &lt;e:translation key="audio-test.instructions" /&gt;
            </pre>
            
        
            <p>
              renders the following text:
          
              Koe sisältää kuullunymmärtämisen tehtäviä.
              
        
            </p>
            
        
            <p>
              For a full list of available translations, 
              <a
                href="https://github.com/digabi/exam-engine/tree/master/packages/core/src/i18n"
              >
                see these files
              </a>
              .
        By default, each exam's translations are first looked up in their corresponding translation files (for example,
        German exam = GA.ts), and then in the generic Finnish/Swedish translation files (fi-FI.ts and sv-FI.ts)
            </p>
            
      
          </div>
          
    
        </div>
        


  
      </div>
    </section>
    

  
